", "stats": {"downloads": 95, "unique_downloads": 94, "views": 367, "unique_views": 353, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 0, "version_views": 0}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-24T18:58:30.523134+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T18:58:30.691371+00:00", "id": 23624429, "conceptrecid": "4317189", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23624429", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.4317189", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624429", "metadata": {"title": "JuliaGNI/SimpleSolvers.jl: v0.14.3", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23624429", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<h2>SimpleSolvers v0.14.3</h2>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/JuliaGNI/SimpleSolvers.jl/compare/v0.14.2...v0.14.3\">Diff since v0.14.2</a></p>\n<h2>Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Julia 1.12 is the floor</strong> (<code>[compat] julia = &quot;1.12&quot;</code>, from 1.11). A patch release, because no\nAPI changes: a caller on Julia 1.11 can no longer install this version.\nThe test in <code>test/quality/jet.jl</code> that checks the <code>Float32</code> and <code>Float16</code> line searches no\nlonger binds <code>one(T)</code> to a local outside the merit closure, a form that existed because a\nclosure capturing <code>T</code> inferred <code>one(T)</code> as <code>Any</code> on Julia 1.11: on 1.12.7 <code>JET.report_opt</code>\nof <code>solve_with_status</code> reports nothing for the closure that calls <code>one(T)</code> itself.</li>\n<li><strong><code>SufficientDecreaseCondition</code> and <code>CurvatureCondition</code> check their numeric argument with\n<code>throw(AssertionError(...))</code> instead of <code>@assert</code></strong> (the constructor check <code>\u03c4 \u2265 0</code> and\n<code>0 &lt; c &lt; 1</code>; the error type and message are unchanged). <code>@assert</code> builds an interpolated\nmessage through a type barrier, which types the <code>AssertionError</code> argument <code>Any</code>, and JET 0.12,\nwhich requires Julia 1.12, reports that construction as a runtime dispatch in\n<code>solve_with_status</code> of <code>Backtracking</code> and <code>StrongWolfe</code> and in <code>solve!</code> of the nonlinear\nsolvers, on every construction of the condition.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Merged pull requests:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Raise the Julia floor to 1.12 (#218) (@michakraus)</li>\n</ul>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Michael Kraus", "affiliation": "Max-Planck-Institut f\u00fcr Plasmaphysik"}, {"name": "benedict-96", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Em Chu", "affiliation": null}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/JuliaGNI/SimpleSolvers.jl/tree/v0.14.3", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "v0.14.3", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/JuliaGNI/SimpleSolvers.jl"}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "mit-license"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 61, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "4317189"}}]}}, "title": "JuliaGNI/SimpleSolvers.jl: v0.14.3", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624429", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23624429", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23624429?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624429", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624429", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23624429", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624429/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/4317189", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/4317189", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4317189", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.4317189", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23624429/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23624429/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23