conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23624407", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624408", "metadata": {"title": "DEA-MP/H: replication package for household multidimensional poverty measurement", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23624408", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<p>Replication package accompanying manuscript version 11 of &ldquo;Pesos end&oacute;genos e monotonicidade na mensura&ccedil;&atilde;o da pobreza multidimensional&rdquo;. DEA-MP/H measures relative multidimensional deprivation at household level using a fixed DEA reference, nested categorical comparison groups, resource share floors and iterative screening of reference households.<br><br>The archive contains the R implementation, a single entry point (run_all.R), variable documentation, aggregate empirical results for the Brazilian Demographic Censuses of 2010 and 2022, robustness analyses, computational checks, execution log and SHA-256 manifests. Census microdata and individual intermediate bases are excluded; the scripts obtain official public inputs from IBGE. Empirical applications illustrate the proposed method.<br><br>Version 1.1.0 corresponds to manuscript v11 (24 October 2026). Code and documentation: MIT license. Repository: https://github.com/moisesluna2026/dea-mp-h</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Brand\u00e3o, Mois\u00e9s Luna", "affiliation": "Escola de Engenharia de S\u00e3o Carlos, Universidade de S\u00e3o Paulo"}, {"name": "Mariano, Enzo Barberio", "affiliation": "Universidade Estadual Paulista (UNESP)"}, {"name": "Rebelatto, Daisy Aparecida do Nascimento", "affiliation": "Escola de Engenharia de S\u00e3o Carlos, Universidade de S\u00e3o Paulo"}], "keywords": ["multidimensional poverty"], "version": "1.1.0", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/moisesluna2026/dea-mp-h", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "r", "title": {"en": "R"}}]}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "mit-license"}, "relat