s.jl: v0.18.7", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23624158", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<h2>GeometricIntegrators v0.18.7</h2>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/JuliaGNI/GeometricIntegrators.jl/compare/v0.18.6...v0.18.7\">Diff since v0.18.6</a></p>\n<h2>Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>Julia 1.12 is the floor</strong> (<code>[compat] julia = &quot;1.12&quot;</code>, from 1.11). A patch release, because no\nAPI changes: a caller on Julia 1.11 can no longer install this version.\nThe repository records no reason for the raise, and the package contains no version-conditional\ncode, so no workaround is removed.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><strong>CI coverage and cache.</strong> CI uploads coverage from the <code>Julia 1 - ubuntu-latest</code> job instead of\n<code>Julia min</code>, and a test job saves the Julia cache only when it succeeds.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Documentation</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Manual figures published by GeometricFigures.jl.</strong> The seven figures in the manual link the\nlight and dark SVGs that GeometricFigures.jl publishes, and <code>docs/make.jl</code> loads its\n<code>figures.css</code>, which shows the SVG that matches the <code>documenter-light</code> or <code>documenter-dark</code>\ntheme. The TikZ sources in <code>docs/src/images/</code>, their <code>Makefile</code> and the <code>images</code> target of\n<code>docs/Makefile</code> are removed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Merged pull requests:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Link the integrator figures from GeometricFigures (#271) (@michakraus)</li>\n<li>CI: coverage from Julia 1 on ubuntu, save the cache only from a job that succeeds (#272) (@michakraus)</li>\n<li>Rename citation keys to the house scheme (#273) (@michakraus)</li>\n<li>Raise the Julia floor to 1.12 (#274) (@michakraus)</li>\n</ul>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Michael Kraus", "affiliation": "Max-Planck-Institut f\u00fcr Plasmaphysik"}, {"name": "Tomasz Tyranowski", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Christopher 