rylov methods, physics-agnostic preconditioners, mixed-precision iterative refinement, and structure-preserving discrete adjoints, all jit/vmap/grad-transparent on CPU and GPU. Releases archive the library together with its benchmark drivers and committed measurement records for independent reproduction.", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Jorge, Rogerio", "affiliation": "University of Wisconsin-Madison"}], "keywords": ["JAX", "linear solvers", "automatic differentiation", "Krylov methods", "preconditioning", "mixed precision", "plasma physics"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21651844", "relation": "isVersionOf", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "v0.33.0", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/uwplasma/SOLVAX"}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "mit-license"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 26, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21651844"}}]}}, "title": "SOLVAX: differentiable structured linear solvers, preconditioners and matrix-free methods in JAX", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23624157", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23624157?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624157", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624157", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23624157", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21651844", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21651844", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21651844", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21651844", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23624157/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23624157/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23624157/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-24T18:35:10.472935+00:00", "recid": "23624157", "revision": 4, "files": [{"id": "dea781c4-c430-49c5-bebf-ac05053dc683", "key": "uwplasma/SOLVAX-v0.33.0.zip", "size": 765069, "checksum": "md5:35bc7694cb851cb45fe470e7a04df86d", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624157/files/uwplasma/SOLVAX-v0.33.0.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "85694"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 59, "unique_downloads": 59, "views": 411, "unique_views": 394, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 0, "version_views": 0}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-24T18:34:35.753583+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T18:34:35.993783+00:00", "id": 23623629, "conceptrecid": "23623628", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23623629", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23623628", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23623629", "metadata": {"title": "Computational experiments on radical towers and their parametrizations: scripts and data", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23623629", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<p>Scripts, data and results of the computational experiments on radical towers and radical parametrizations accompanying the paper \"On the structure of radical towers and their parametrizations\" by J. Sendra-Arranz, J. R. Sendra and J. Sendra.</p>\n<p>On twelve radical towers with 3, 5, 7 and 10 floors, the classical computation of the tower variety and of the radical variety of a radical parametrization is compared with the methods introduced in the paper: the irreducibility of the incidence variety, the isomorphic tower whose tower variety is obtained without elimination (Algorithm 1), and the minimal radical subtower of a parametrization (Algorithms 2 and 3).</p>\n<p>The archive contains the report describing the experiments and its results (PDF and LaTeX source), the definition of the twelve towers and their parametrizations, the Singular scripts of all the methods and of the certification of the towers, Python scripts to generate the Singular scripts, run the experiments and verify the results, the timings of every computation and the ideals computed. The computations were carried out with Singular 4.3.2.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Sendra-Arranz, Javier", "affiliation": "CUNEF Universidad"}, {"name": "Sendra, Juan Rafael", "affiliation": "CUNEF Universidad"}, {"name": "Sendra, Juana", "affiliation": "CUNEF Universidad"}], "keywords": ["radical parametrization", "radical tower", "tower variety", "radical variety", "minimal radical parametrization", "Gr\u00f6bner bases", "elimination", "Singular"], "version": "1.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23623628"}}]}}, "title": "Computational experiments on radical towers and their parametrizations: scripts and data", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23623629", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23623629?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23623629", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23623629", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23623629", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623628", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23623628", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23623628", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23623628", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23623629/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23623629/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23623629/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-24T18:34:35.993783+00:00", "recid": "23623629", "revision": 4, "files": [{"id": "074da745-38d8-4f2e-a948-d9a2b1cb29bb", "key": "radical-towers-experiments.zip", "size": 1348824, "checksum": "md5:8ad9fb7b7c962be224a7c5aa73d7b27d", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23623629/files/radical-towers-experiments.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1921844"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 0, "unique_downloads": 0, "views": 0, "unique_views": 0, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 0, "version_views": 0}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-24T18:32:02.147009+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T18:39:16.239168+00:00", "id": 23624089, "conceptrecid": "23497613", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23624089", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23497613", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624089", "metadata": {"title": "Code and data for: How much of the efficiency lost to receiver degradation can internal heat transfer enhancement recover? An upper bound for parabolic trough collectors", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23624089", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<p>Python model, Sandia LS-2 validation data, simulation results, automated tests and figure scripts for the manuscript &ldquo;How much of the efficiency lost to receiver degradation can internal heat transfer enhancement recover? An upper bound for parabolic trough collectors&rdquo;, submitted to Thermal Science and Engineering Progress. Version 3 adds the hydrogen-annulus model and the plant-level impact calculation. The code was developed with the assistance of an AI tool (Claude, Anthropic) and was checked and rerun by the author.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Elmnefi, Muhammed", "affiliation": "Ostim Technical University", "orcid": "0000-0001-5956-0537"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 2, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23497613"}}]}}, "title": "Code and data for: How much of the efficiency lost to receiver degradation can internal heat transfer enhancement recover? An upper bound for parabolic trough collectors", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23624089", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23624089?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624089", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624089", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23624089", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23497613", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23497613", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23497613", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23497613", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23624089/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23624089/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23624089/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-24T18:39:16.239168+00:00", "recid": "23624089", "revision": 8, "files": [{"id": "56c3d7ea-5318-4aff-82a5-9a97972843ab", "key": "ptc_model (5).zip", "size": 5538786, "checksum": "md5:1a1a61cd086bd99c4ad5acd5668f305e", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624089/files/ptc_model%20(5).zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1953468"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 3, "unique_downloads": 3, "views": 11, "unique_views": 8, "version_downloads": 0, "version_unique_downloads": 0, "version_unique_views": 0, "version_views": 0}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-24T18:31:39.839462+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T18:31:39.984613+00:00", "id": 23624050, "conceptrecid": "16897616", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23624050", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.16897616", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23624050", "metadata": {"title": "HIMS-CDI Synthetic Data Archive", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23624050", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<p>HIMS-CDI Synthetic Data Archive<br>Companion to: \"HIMS-CDI: A Governance Specification and Assurance Architecture for CTI-Driven Cybersecurity Risk Assessment in Healthcare\"</p>\n<p>This archive contains the production synthetic-data pipeline, the prespecified correlation matrix, and the labelled 240-environment dataset used in the Phase I specification-validation study reported in Section 4 of the manuscript.</p>\n<p>The synthetic corpus comprises 240 healthcare cybersecurity environments, each characterised by 20 indicators across five groups (CTI Modality, Semantic Enrichment, Fusion Strategy, Regulatory Traceability, Explainability). The pipeline applies empirical marginal transformations (beta, categorical), generates labels via the three non-compensatory governance gates (CDI &ge; 0.70, CCR &ge; 0.80, latency &lt; 200 ms, memory &lt; 100 MB), injects Gaussian noise (&sigma; = 0.13), and performs a stratified 60/20/20 split (seed 123). The test split yields exactly 48 environments (32 NOT_DEPLOY_SYNTH, 16 DEPLOY_SYNTH), matching the manuscript's specification.</p>\n<p>Random seeds: 42 = corpus generation; 123 = stratified split; 10-seed sweep = model-training runs.</p>\n<p>Provenance: The correlation matrix is a prespecified design parameter, not an empirical estimate. MITRE ATT&amp;CK v14.1 technique frequencies and dwell-time parameters (mean 62 days, SD 28 days) are prespecified simulation assumptions, not observed healthcare incident statistics.</p>\n<p>Epistemic boundary: This archive supports Phase I specification testing only. It does not contain real healthcare incident data, and the synthetic evaluation does not establish clinical safety, operational effectiveness, real-world predictive validity, or operational deployment readiness. Phase II validation against real healthcare incident outcomes is planned (see manuscript Section 6.2&ndash;6.3).</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Akeredolu, Oluseun", "affiliation": "University of Warwick", "orcid": "0009-0009-3773-0465"}], "keywords": ["Cybersecurity", "Healthcare", "Synthetic Data", "Governance", "Machine Learning"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/oluseun-akeredolu/HIMS-CDI/tree/phase1-v1.0", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.5.4", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/oluseun-akeredolu/HIMS-CDI"}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "apache2.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 16, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "16897616"}}]}, "notes": "<p># HIMS-CDI Training Pipeline &mdash; Zenodo Archive Change Log</p>\n<p>**Zenodo Record:** [10.5281/zenodo.23586311](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23586311)<br>**GitHub Repository:** [oluseun-akeredolu/HIMS-CDI](https://github.com/oluseun-akeredolu/HIMS-CDI)</p>\n<p>---</p>\n<p>## Version 1.4.0 &mdash; 2026-10-23</p>\n<p>**Source commit:** `84247ca` &mdash; *\"Final v9.4 verifier: all gate checks (per-case and mean) use shared function\"*</p>\n<p>**Archive file:** `training_pipeline.zip` (82,084 bytes)<br>**Archive MD5:** `d30deaacde5d4971bb2975126ebaf521`<br>**File count:** 31 files in `training_pipeline/`</p>\n<p>### Reason for new version</p>\n<p>The previous version (v1.3.2) shipped an incomplete and inconsistent snapshot of the training pipeline. Two structural defects made the archive non-runnable as published:</p>\n<p>1. **`governance_gates.py` was completely missing** from the archive. This file is the canonical single-source-of-truth for the four non-compensatory governance gates (CDI &ge; 0.70, CCR &ge; 0.80, latency &lt; 200 ms, memory &lt; 100 MB) and is imported by `verify_outputs.py` and `tests/test_governance_gates.py`. Without it, neither file could execute against the archive.<br>2. **`verify_outputs.py` was an older (v9.3-era) version** that performed gate threshold checks with inline `if cdi_mean &gt;= 0.70` comparisons, bypassing the shared gate function. This contradicted the v9.4 manuscript claim that all gate decisions &mdash; per-case and on the mean &mdash; go through a single shared function.</p>\n<p>Version 1.4.0 fixes both issues and re-aligns the Zenodo archive with the current `main` branch of the GitHub repository.</p>\n<p>### Summary of changes</p>\n<p>| Category | Count |<br>|---|---|<br>| Files added | 5 |<br>| Files removed | 3 |<br>| Files with substantive content changes | 9 |<br>| Files with line-ending normalisation only (CRLF &rarr; LF) | 14 |<br>| **Total files in new archive** | **31** (was 28) |</p>\n<p>### Files added in v1.4.0</p>\n<p>| Path | Bytes | Purpose |<br>|---|---|---|<br>| `training_pipeline/governance_gates.py` | 2,709 | **Canonical single-source-of-truth for the four governance gates.** Was missing in v1.3.2; required by `verify_outputs.py` and `tests/test_governance_gates.py`. |<br>| `training_pipeline/tests/test_governance_gates.py` | 4,995 | 15 pytest cases covering boundary behaviour (e.g. CDI = 0.70 passes; latency = 200 ms fails; memory = 100 MB fails; fail-closed on invalid input). Referenced by the manuscript as RQ2 endpoint 1. |<br>| `training_pipeline/tests/__init__.py` | 58 | Package marker for `tests/`. |<br>| `training_pipeline/bootstrap/bootstrap_ensemble.py` | 4,277 | Stratified case-bootstrap on ensemble-averaged probabilities (10 000 resamples). Used by `run_training.py`. |<br>| `training_pipeline/results/run_manifest.json` | 789 | Run provenance: dataset DOI, training-pipeline DOI, Python/library versions, model-training seeds, classification threshold, bootstrap method, gate-logic-test count. |<br>| `training_pipeline/results/test_output.txt` | 627 | Captured stdout of the most recent `verify_outputs.py` run for transparency. |</p>\n<p>### Files removed in v1.4.0</p>\n<p>| Path | Bytes | Reason |<br>|---|---|---|<br>| `training_pipeline/results/threshold_sensitivity.json` | 4,592 | Regenerated result file; superseded by the canonical JSON kept in the GitHub repository. Removed from the Zenodo archive to avoid shipping stale regenerated artefacts. |<br>| `training_pipeline/results/weight_sensitivity.json` | 49,009 | Same as above. |<br>| `training_pipeline/results/workstation_resource_usage.csv` | 6,330 | Same as above. |</p>\n<p>These three files remain available in the GitHub repository for anyone who needs the regenerated sensitivity sweeps; they were excluded from the Zenodo archive because Zenodo archives should hold a single canonical run, not regenerated sweeps that vary with the host environment.</p>\n<p>### Files with substantive content changes</p>\n<p>| Path | Old size (v1.3.2) | New size (v1.4.0) | Nature of change |<br>|---|---|---|---|<br>| `training_pipeline/verify_outputs.py` | 7,312 | 11,145 | **Major rewrite** to delegate all gate evaluations to `evaluate_governance_gates()` from the new shared module. Removes every inline `if cdi_mean &gt;= 0.70` comparison. The mean-block now reports `FAIL &mdash; CCR gate(s) fail` based on the shared function's `CCR_pass` boolean, not a hardcoded string. Adds Table 7 metric-match comparison, gate-satisfaction match against the shared function, run-manifest check, and separates RQ2 into two endpoints (logic tests + scenario pass rate). |<br>| `training_pipeline/run_training.py` | 17,483 | 11,212 | Refactor: removes inline gate-threshold comparisons; calls `evaluate_governance_gates()` from `governance_gates.py`. Updated to use stratified case-bootstrap on ensemble-averaged probabilities (10 000 resamples, seed 42). Updated result-file writing to include `run_manifest.json`. |<br>| `training_pipeline/measurement/workstation_measure.py` | 2,559 | 2,510 | Refactored to use `psutil` for memory measurement; removed inline `if mem &lt; 100` logic. |<br>| `training_pipeline/configs/seeds.yaml` | 1,722 | 1,526 | Cleaned up: removed dead keys, kept only the values actually read by `run_training.py`. |<br>| `training_pipeline/requirements.txt` | 552 | 168 | Trimmed to actual runtime deps. Removed `memory-profiler`, `tqdm`, `onnx`, `onnxruntime` (the latter two were already commented out). Added `pytest&gt;=7.0` for the new `tests/` directory. |<br>| `training_pipeline/results/per_seed_predictions.csv` | 182,750 | 176,493 | Regenerated from the canonical 10-seed &times; 9-model &times; 48-case run (4,320 rows). |<br>| `training_pipeline/results/table5_resource_usage.csv` | 552 | 14,313 | Expanded: now includes per-seed resource measurements and a column for the canonical mean &plusmn; SD reported in the manuscript. |<br>| `training_pipeline/results/table7_classification.csv` | 746 | 853 | Regenerated with the corrected bootstrap (stratified case-bootstrap on ensemble-averaged probabilities); now includes 95 % CIs for AUROC and macro-F1. |<br>| `training_pipeline/results/gate_satisfaction.csv` | 5,016 | 5,468 | Regenerated using the shared `evaluate_governance_gates()` function. Per-case gate decisions are now guaranteed to match the shared function's output. |<br>| `training_pipeline/results/bootstrap_ci.json` | 4,937 | 3,233 | Updated to reflect the new stratified case-bootstrap method. |</p>\n<p>### Files with line-ending normalisation only</p>\n<p>The following 14 files are unchanged in content; only their line endings were normalised from CRLF (Windows) to LF (Unix) to match the GitHub `main` branch:</p>\n<p>- `training_pipeline/README.md`<br>- `training_pipeline/bootstrap/__init__.py`<br>- `training_pipeline/bootstrap/rubin_pooling.py`<br>- `training_pipeline/calibration/__init__.py`<br>- `training_pipeline/calibration/platt_scaling.py`<br>- `training_pipeline/measurement/__init__.py`<br>- `training_pipeline/measurement/pi_measure.py`<br>- `training_pipeline/models/__init__.py`<br>- `training_pipeline/models/baselines.py`<br>- `training_pipeline/models/edge_aware_fusion.py`<br>- `training_pipeline/models/gnn.py`<br>- `training_pipeline/models/mlr_platt.py`<br>- `training_pipeline/models/transformer.py`<br>- `training_pipeline/threshold_sensitivity.py`<br>- `training_pipeline/weight_sensitivity.py`</p>\n<p>### Integrity verification</p>\n<p>After extracting the new archive, the following MD5 hashes should match. If they do not, the archive has been corrupted in transit.</p>\n<p>| File | Expected MD5 |<br>|---|---|<br>| `training_pipeline/governance_gates.py` | `881de51a10be54435649a309e8302fb9` |<br>| `training_pipeline/verify_outputs.py` | `ea98cdbbfb06f5429bb5ebd55fa94b77` |<br>| `training_pipeline.zip` (whole archive) | `d30deaacde5d4971bb2975126ebaf521` |</p>\n<p>### Runtime verification</p>\n<p>The new archive has been tested end-to-end:</p>\n<p>1. Extract `training_pipeline.zip` to a clean directory.<br>2. Install dependencies: `pip install -r training_pipeline/requirements.txt`.<br>3. Download the synthetic data archive from [10.5281/zenodo.23565580](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23565580) and unpack to a directory `&lt;archive&gt;`.<br>4. Run:</p>\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp;```bash<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;cd training_pipeline<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;python verify_outputs.py --results-dir results --archive-dir &lt;archive&gt;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;```</p>\n<p>5. Expected final line: `Verification: ALL CHECKS PASSED` followed by the four separate research findings (RQ1 sensitivity, RQ2 decision logic, RQ2 scenario-level, memory gate).</p>\n<p>### Provenance</p>\n<p>| Field | Value |<br>|---|---|<br>| Source repository | `https://github.com/oluseun-akeredolu/HIMS-CDI` |<br>| Source commit | `84247caa734a2554fd9f4e4551760691a4fafce0` |<br>| Commit subject | *Final v9.4 verifier: all gate checks (per-case and mean) use shared function* |<br>| Commit author | Oluseun Akeredolu &lt;Olu.Akeredolu@warwick.ac.uk&gt; |<br>| Commit date | 2026-10-23 |<br>| Build method | `git archive --format=tar origin/main -- training_pipeline/` then `zip -r` |<br>| Build date | 2026-10-23 |</p>\n<p>---</p>\n<p>## Version 1.3.2 &mdash; 2026-10-23 (superseded)</p>\n<p>**Archive file:** `training_pipeline.zip` (88,413 bytes)<br>**File count:** 28 files in `training_pipeline/`</p>\n<p>This version is preserved on Zenodo for citation continuity but is **not runnable** as published, because `governance_gates.py` is missing and `verify_outputs.py` uses inline threshold logic that bypasses the canonical gate function. Users should switch to v1.4.0 for any execution or replication.</p>"}, "title": "HIMS-CDI Synthetic Data Archive", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23624050", "self_html": "https://z